	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[Orgrimmar is the capital of the {link:horde}Horde{/link}, a fortress city in the mountains of northern {link:durotar}Durotar{/link}. Its walls are of timber, stone and iron, and much of it is carved into the red rock of the canyons. Through its great gate pass {link:orcs}orc{/link} warriors, troll hunters, {link:tauren}tauren{/link} elders and the pale envoys of the {link:forsaken}Forsaken{/link}. At its heart sits the hall of the Warchief. The city bears the name of {link:orgrim-doomhammer}Orgrim Doomhammer{/link}, who died so that his people might be free, and it is meant to show the world what the orcs have become: not a war machine of demons, but a nation.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[When the war against the {link:burning-legion}Burning Legion{/link} was won, {link:thrall}Thrall{/link} brought his people to the eastern coast of {link:kalimdor}Kalimdor{/link} and set about building a home for them. He chose a site where the northern mountains would guard the city's back, and he named it for Doomhammer, his friend and teacher. The orcs did not raise it alone. The {link:tauren}tauren{/link}, the {link:darkspear-trolls}Darkspear{/link} and the goblins lent their hands, and the city rose quickly, valley by valley. Even as it was built, the humans of {link:kul-tiras}Kul Tiras{/link} came to tear it down. They failed, and Orgrimmar stood.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Present Day",
			text = [=[Orgrimmar is the greatest city of the {link:horde}Horde{/link}, and its heart. {link:thrall}Thrall{/link} rules from {link:grommash-hold}Grommash Hold{/link}, with the chieftain of the {link:darkspear-trolls}Darkspear{/link} and his old counselors at his side. Its markets are loud, its training halls are full, and its young warriors hunger for their first battle. But the city has enemies within its walls. The cultists of the {link:burning-blade}Burning Blade{/link} whisper in the {link:cleft-of-shadow}Cleft of Shadow{/link}, and beneath the city, in the burning caves of {link:ragefire-chasm}Ragefire Chasm{/link}, a sect of the {link:shadow-council}Shadow Council{/link} gathers its strength. Thrall knows more of them than they believe.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Inhabitants",
			text = [=[• {b}The orcs.{/b} Warriors, shaman, smiths and traders, free of the demon's curse and proud of it.
• {b}The {link:darkspear-trolls}Darkspear{/link} trolls.{/b} They keep their own quarter in the {link:valley-of-spirits}Valley of Spirits{/link}.
• {b}The {link:tauren}tauren{/link}.{/b} Elders and travellers from {link:thunder-bluff}Thunder Bluff{/link}, allies of the Warchief.
• {b}The {link:forsaken}Forsaken{/link}.{/b} Envoys of {link:sylvanas-windrunner}Sylvanas Windrunner{/link}, newly accepted into the {link:horde}Horde{/link} and watched with some unease.
• {b}The goblins.{/b} Merchants and engineers who serve anyone who pays.
• {b}The {link:burning-blade}Burning Blade{/link}.{/b} Hidden among the rest, as the rot hides in a sound timber.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[• {b}The Founding.{/b} The city was raised after the {link:battle-of-mount-hyjal}Battle of Mount Hyjal{/link}, while the orcs tamed the lands around it and drove off {link:quilboar}quilboar{/link}, {link:centaurs}centaur{/link} and harpies.
• {b}The Admiral's War.{/b} The fleet of {link:daelin-proudmoore}Daelin Proudmoore{/link} threatened the new city from the sea. The {link:horde}Horde{/link} broke the admiral's keep and slew him at {link:theramore-isle}Theramore{/link}.
• {b}The Present Day.{/b} The Horde has grown to include the {link:forsaken}Forsaken{/link} of {link:lordaeron}Lordaeron{/link}, and Orgrimmar has become the meeting place of all its peoples.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Lore of the City",
			text = [=[• The Warchief's fortress is named {link:grommash-hold}Grommash Hold{/link}, for {link:grom-hellscream}Grom Hellscream{/link}, who slew the demon {link:mannoroth}Mannoroth{/link} and freed the orcs from the blood curse.
• When a hero of the {link:horde}Horde{/link} brings home the head of a great enemy, it is raised in the {link:valley-of-strength}Valley of Strength{/link} for all the city to see.
• In the tavern of the Valley of Strength drinks a {link:tauren}tauren{/link} named {link:gamon}Gamon{/link}. He serves a troll who trades with the pirates of the southern coast, and he is rarely sober.
• The rogues of the city say that a society called the Shattered Hand works in the shadows of the Cleft, and that it believes the Warchief is too cautious.]=],
		},
	},
})

