		},
		{
			title = "Significance",
			text = [=[Through Vol'jin, the {link:trolls}trolls{/link} have become a true people of the {link:horde}Horde{/link} and not only its allies. He is proof that the Horde of {link:thrall}Thrall{/link} is a league of free peoples.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Oath of Sen'jin",
			text = [=[The {link:darkspear-trolls}Darkspear{/link} were outcasts, driven from the jungles and scattered across the islands of the southern seas. When a storm cast {link:thrall}Thrall{/link}'s fleet upon their shores, the tribe was fighting for its life against humans and the murlocs of the deep. Thrall fought beside the trolls. Their chieftain, Sen'jin, was taken by the murlocs and did not return, but he had foreseen that the orcish warchief would lead his people to a new home. Sen'jin's son swore the tribe to the {link:horde}Horde{/link}.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Isles and the Traitor",
			text = [=[After the war against the Legion, the {link:darkspear-trolls}Darkspear{/link} settled the {link:echo-isles}Echo Isles{/link} off the coast of {link:durotar}Durotar{/link}. Their peace was short. The fleet of {link:kul-tiras}Kul Tiras{/link} fell upon the isles, and Vol'jin had to see his people evacuated while the {link:horde}Horde{/link} struck back at the human ships. Then came a worse blow: {link:zalazane}Zalazane{/link}, a witch doctor of their own tribe, turned his magic against them. The free Darkspear fled to the mainland and built a village there, which they named for Sen'jin.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Deeds",
